Part 4. Proposition 3.10: two tests with values in [0, 1]; questions are vectors v in [-1, 1]^2
   b_k(v, 1) = max(v_k, 0), b_k(v, 0) = max(-v_k, 0); the human gives the answer the imitator does not give;
   the adversary's v is orthogonal to the books and has maximum norm 1 (floating point)
